 24. TUTOR: Okay, perfect. Sounds good.\nTurn 25. TUTOR: All right, are you ready?\nTurn 26. STUDENT: Yeah.\nTurn 27. TUTOR: All right. Let me know if she's not paying at- last time she fell asleep.\nTurn 28. TUTOR: Oh, okay, okay, okay, okay.\nTurn 29. TUTOR: Yeah. So...\nTurn 30. TUTOR: Okay.\nTurn 31. TUTOR: After soccer camp, that's why she went missing and that's what...\nTurn 32. TUTOR: It's fine. I was at home, so I don't know.\nTurn 33. TUTOR: But she will be wide awake and ready today and if she doesn't listen or participate, she will not be going to a play date, so...\nTurn 34. TUTOR: Full attention she's got you.\nTurn 35. TUTOR: Okay. It's it's okay.\nTurn 36. TUTOR: I think... Thank you.\nTurn 37. TUTOR: Yeah, no problem. Okay.\nTurn 38. TUTOR: How are you doing, Mia?\nTurn 39. STUDENT: Good.\nTurn 40. TUTOR: Was that nap good last time?\nTurn 41. STUDENT: Mmm.\nTurn 42. TUTOR: Yeah.\nTurn 43. TUTOR: Don't worry about it. It's okay. I didn't know if you got hurt or anything, but now that I know it's just a nap, it's okay.\nTurn 44. TUTOR: Uh, yeah, let's just like try staying on the camera this time. Does that sound good? That way I could in case you do fall asleep, then I could just know, oh, it's just 'cause she fell asleep, not 'cause, oh, you know.\nTurn 45. STUDENT: Yeah.\nTurn 46. TUTOR: Okay. So I'll start sharing my screen.\nTurn 47. TUTOR: All right. I'm a little sick right now, so my voice is um not doing the best, but mhm.\nTurn 48. TUTOR: I can't present. Okay.\nTurn 49. TUTOR: There you go. Is it on the screen now?\nTurn 50. STUDENT: Yeah.\nTurn 51. TUTOR: Okay, sounds good.\nTurn 52. TUTOR: So, did you want a few minutes to rest or you ready to go?\nTurn 53. STUDENT: I'm ready to go.\nTurn 54. TUTOR: Okay. Um, yeah, so it sounds like we're gonna be doing addition and subtraction again. Um, let's see. You think you can do the two-digit subtraction pretty good?\nTurn 55. STUDENT: Yeah.\nTurn 56. TUTOR: Okay, let's do it again. Does that soun